  {
    "sha": "87cf32dd85f7d3c2f8a937c8e720a0e271e43130",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDg3Y2YzMmRkODVmN2QzYzJmOGE5MzdjOGU3MjBhMGUyNzFlNDMxMzA",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-19T10:49:27Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-19T10:49:27Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(import): divide the boundary edges of faces curved two ways finer\n\n#2731 made the STEP chord report true: the highest kept facet edge times\nthe face kind's inside bound. The fit never splits a boundary edge, and the\nkernel held those edges only to the pass tolerance, so each model with a\ncone, sphere or torus face read 1.5 x the tolerance and became reduced\nfidelity (fig8: 0.00749 mm, three shoulder_adaptive tests red).\n\nEach shell edge is now divided before the pass by the largest inside bound\nof its faces (step_fit::edge_divisors, CurveGuard::finer), once in the\nshell's own polyline, so the shell stays closed. A cylinder carries its\nfinest rim's divisor to all its edges, so its wall still meshes rim to rim.\nfig8 now reads 0.005 mm (full fidelity), 7822 -> 7974 facets.\n\nFixes #2754\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "e4279659678a98606ea641d789810b535fbde9fe",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/trees/e4279659678a98606ea641d789810b535fbde9fe"
      },
